{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sg4BeffKpGKQJYUTWWuoBT","type":"tool_result","content":"A search costs **2 credits per 10 results**, rounded up per block of 10. For example, 11 results cost 4 credits.\n\nOn top of that, each result that gets scraped adds per-page scrape costs. Scrape option surcharges stack on each page, so JSON format adds 4 credits per scraped page. Enhanced proxy adds nothing, since it bills at the same 1 credit as a basic request, and an escalated retry is not charged again.\n\nFor example, 10 results with JSON format on every page would cost 2 + 10 × (1 + 4) = 52 credits. The source doesn't explicitly confirm whether the 1-credit base applies to each scraped result, so treat that figure as an estimate."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17c3c212-9e3b-42ca-8feb-0f9268acf886","uuid":"dd89ab9d-94a1-4ae8-b917-e0837c8b04de","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:42:36.280Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":24447,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"A search costs **2 credits per 10 results**, rounded up per block of 10. For example, 11 results cost 4 credits.\n\nOn top of that, each result that gets scraped adds per-page scrape costs. Scrape option surcharges stack on each page, so JSON format adds 4 credits per scraped page. Enhanced proxy adds nothing, since it bills at the same 1 credit as a basic request, and an escalated retry is not charged again.\n\nFor example, 10 results with JSON format on every page would cost 2 + 10 × (1 + 4) = 52 credits. The source doesn't explicitly confirm whether the 1-credit base applies to each scraped result, so treat that figure as an estimate.","durationMs":4871,"url":"https://docs.firecrawl.dev/billing"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Sg4BeffKpGKQJYUTWWuoBT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73Dy2QS4i3xei6mUvTZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A Firecrawl search costs **2 credits per 10 results**, rounded up to the next block of 10. For example, 11 results cost 4 credits.\n\nIf you also scrape the result pages, each scraped page adds its own scrape cost on top:\n- The JSON format adds 4 credits per scraped page.\n- Enhanced proxy adds nothing extra, because it bills at the same 1 credit as a basic request. An escalated retry isn't charged again.\n\nFor example, 10 results with JSON format on every page would cost about 2 + 10 × (1 + 4) = 52 credits. That figure is an estimate. The billing page I checked doesn't explicitly say the 1-credit base applies to each scraped result.\n\nThe source is https://docs.firecrawl.dev/billing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":18642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"output_tokens":253,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17c3c212-9e3b-42ca-8feb-0f9268acf886","uuid":"3b67f762-89ea-4a61-8778-a9e3bce0b4b8","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:42:38.473Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73Dxozdaaq85qtprvgB"}
